                <pb facs="0123" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0046B/a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-04T23:00:00-04:00">February 4,
                            1943—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>840. In view of decision by this Government to construct additional refining
                    facilities at Bahrein involving substantial increase in American personnel and
                    shipping there, the Department desires to establish a consulate at Bahrein. In
                    as much as the foreign affairs of Bahrein are controlled by the British
                    Government please ascertain whether the appropriate British authorities are
                    agreeable to the establishment of the consulate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
